index 66844ad..d20c655 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -51,6 +51,10 @@ npm install dayjs --save
 
 📚[Installation Guide](https://day.js.org/docs/en/installation/installation)
 
+#### TypeScript
+
+Type declarations are bundled, so no `@types/dayjs` package is needed. They require **TypeScript 3.2 or later**: `types/plugin/bigIntSupport.d.ts` refers to the `BigInt` global, which TypeScript first shipped in 3.2, and `types/plugin/minMax.d.ts` uses the non-empty tuple type `[Dayjs, ...Dayjs[]]` introduced in 3.0. Your `lib` must include `esnext.bigint` or `es2020` for the `bigIntSupport` declaration to resolve.
+
 ### API
 
 It's easy to use Day.js APIs to parse, validate, manipulate, and display dates and times.
